[{"code":"view_changes_model","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":30,"col":8},"end":{"line":30,"col":19}},"title":"VIEW CHANGES THE MODEL","message":"`view` changes `model.pinned` in place, but the runtime hands `view` the model\nto read only.\n\n30|main = Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → { pinned = [], recent = [] }, update = update, view = view }\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^ the runtime hands `view` the model here\n\nThe runtime keeps the model it hands `view` for the next message and the next\nrender, so a change in place would be seen by both.\n\nLet `view` build a new list instead, or change a copy: `List.copy model.pinned`.\n\nThis is the platform's rule for `view`, whether or not anything else reads the\nlist."}]
